 ### [Hierarchical Ray Marching](5238-hierarchical-ray-marching.md)
-Hierarchical Ray Marching is a sparse voxel traversal technique that dynamically switches between octree node traversal and direct voxel sampling to optimize ray-marching performance. It differs from fixed-leaf or constant-node approaches by adapting the traversal granularity (level) based on whether the ray is currently inside or outside occupied space, allowing it to skip empty regions rapidly at coarse levels and sample details precisely at fine levels.
+Hierarchical Ray Marching is a sparse voxel traversal technique that dynamically switches between octree levels and voxel levels to optimize ray-marching performance. It differs from sibling methods by adjusting the traversal granularity up or down based on hit/miss status, allowing rapid skipping of empty regions at coarse levels and precise sampling at fine levels.
 
